From de2a944657fa5b296d09f631071b478e2ae74af5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prateek <prateekxd15@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:28:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(live): live clipping in the app: sessions API, live
 worker, hook-first clips

POST /live/sessions starts clipping a live YouTube/Twitch stream (one
active session per user, the URL must be live now). A new live-worker
container claims the session, records it into the rolling buffer, flags
streamer reactions with the voice pass, cuts a hook-first window (at most
6 s before the reaction, runs while the streamer talks, 12-30 s, >= 50%
talking), checks the streamer is on camera and moving (facecam layouts),
writes a quick preview, then renders the clip through the normal engine
with the gaming layout and streamer-only captions. Clips and rejections
(with the reason) land in live_clips; GET /live/sessions/{id} polls them,
/live/clips/{id}/file serves the MP4s. Everything is behind LIVE_CLIPPING
(default off: every route 403s except /live/status, the worker idles).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
